  "oracleBeforeTheAbiFix": {
   "why": "Superseded within the hour, and the reason is worth keeping. PrimeOracle.latest() returned a member named `at`, which is a good Solidity name and is also Array.prototype.at. ethers v6 decodes a return tuple into an array-like Result, so `result.at` resolved to the array method, the Repo screen did arithmetic on a function, and the error read 'Cannot convert function to a BigInt' with nothing pointing at the ABI. Renaming it to publishedAt changes the ABI, so the three contracts holding it went up again. HederaRateFeed did not move: it has no such member and the new oracle was pointed at the address already deployed.",
